orner and currently capturable — and once taken, it\'s mine forever.\n\nFurthermore, taking H8 also flips H7, strengthening the entire bottom row.\n\n(F,7) is decent — gains two central pieces, but doesn\'t secure a corner.\n\nBest move: (H,8) — secures the corner, which is strategically superior.\n\nEven though (A,7) flips more pieces, the corner is more valuable.\n\nIn fact, standard Reversi AI often prioritizes corners when available.\n\nMoreover, after taking H8, the opponent may have fewer options.\n\nThus, best choice is (H,8).\n\nReason: Securing a corner provides long-term positional advantage and stability, outweighing short-term gains from flipping more pieces elsewhere. (H,8) is a valid move that captures the valuable corner square and flips an adjacent opponent piece, consolidating control of the bottom row.\n\nAnswer: (H,8)'}
